  "summary": "Added agent ID to HTTP transport session creation for better session identification. The change imports Config and uses `getAgentId()` to create more descriptive session titles (`nezha-{agentId}` instead of fixed `nezha-agent-session`).",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "Test Coverage",
      "reminder": "When adding new functionality to transport layer, always create or update corresponding test file (e.g., transport.test.ts). HttpTransport has no dedicated test file - create one for session creation and message sending."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Import Patterns",
      "reminder": "When using Config, import from '../../config/Config.js' (with .js extension) to match the pattern used in this codebase."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Global Config Access",
      "reminder": "Config uses singleton pattern - use Config.getInstance().getMethod() to access config values. The agentId can come from session context or config file."
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "type": "Missing Test Coverage",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "HttpTransport.doCreateSession() method lacks direct unit tests. While used indirectly in UnifiedAgent tests, no test validates the session title format with agentId."
    },
    {
      "type": "Potential Runtime Issue",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "If Config.getInstance().getAgentId() returns undefined/null, the session title would be 'nezha-undefined' or 'nezha-null'. Consider adding fallback."
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Add HttpTransport unit tests covering: createSession(), sendMessage(), and doCreateSession() specifically for the agentId integration",
